From 006490a9963e29555b0d50b8dcb81ce6f95c884f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jarojarojaro-jaro <miki.jaroszek@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:58:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 27/65] CUDA/HIP: GDN gated output norm silu(z) * (rms_norm(x)
 * w) + q8_1 in one launch (GGML_HIP_NORM_GATE)

RMS_NORM -> MUL(w) -> [reshape of z] -> UNARY_SILU(z) -> MUL becomes rms_norm_mul_silu_gate_f32<NCOLS>: one thread per
column (NCOLS 32..256), one block per row, DPP reductions, writes dst and the q8_1 copy for the out projection.
Bitwise equal to rms_norm_f32<256, true> + unary_gated_op_kernel<op_silu>: the 256-thread kernel sums x^2 of
threads < NCOLS plus zeros, i.e. the same pairings; products are kept out of fma contraction
(ggml_cuda_no_contract) where the two-kernel version could not contract them.

rocprofv3 (Qwen3.8-27B, MTP n=4, verify): rms_norm<256> 2.68 us + unary_gated 1.84 us + one boundary -> 1.87 us,
48 per verify; verify 911 -> 863 kernels, gaps 3.02 -> 2.86 ms, wall 27.79 -> 27.52 ms.
Greedy md5 (plain and MTP) equal to 9f83f1f81. test-backend-ops RMS_NORM_GATE 15/15 (new: NCOLS 32..512, z through a
reshape as in qwen35).
